id: LOG-010
ilities: [analysability]
source: cpm
maturity: 3
action: advisory
title: String concatenation in structured logger
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .js .java .py
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/
patterns:
  - regex: logger\.(info|warn|error|debug|log)\(['"`].*\s*\+\s
    message: "String concatenation in logger — defeats structured logging and wastes CPU on disabled log levels"
  - regex: log\.(info|warn|error|debug)\(['"`].*\s*\+\s
    message: "String concatenation in log call — use structured logging with parameters instead"
fix: Use structured parameters. Node: logger.info({userId, action}, 'msg'). Java: log.info("User {} did {}", userId, action). Python: logger.info('msg', extra={'user': userId}).
